---
config:
  theme: default
title: Analytics Dashboard Sequence
---
sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant AnalyticsPage
    participant API
    participant Backend
    participant MongoDB
    participant Aggregation
    
    %% Load Analytics Dashboard
    Note over User,Aggregation: Load Analytics Dashboard
    User->>AnalyticsPage: Navigate to /analytics
    AnalyticsPage->>User: Show loading skeleton
    
    par Fetch all analytics in parallel
        AnalyticsPage->>API: GET /api/analytics/applications-stats
        API->>Backend: Request application stats
        Backend->>Aggregation: Aggregate applications by status
        Aggregation->>MongoDB: Pipeline:<br/>$match userId<br/>$group by status<br/>$count
        MongoDB-->>Aggregation: Status counts
        Aggregation-->>Backend: {Applied: 15, Interview: 5, ...}
        Backend-->>API: 200 OK + stats
        API-->>AnalyticsPage: Application stats
    and
        AnalyticsPage->>API: GET /api/analytics/hiring-trends
        API->>Backend: Request trends
        Backend->>Aggregation: Aggregate jobs by week
        Aggregation->>MongoDB: Pipeline:<br/>$match last 3 months<br/>$group by week<br/>$count postings
        MongoDB-->>Aggregation: Weekly counts
        Aggregation-->>Backend: Time series data
        Backend-->>API: 200 OK + trends
        API-->>AnalyticsPage: Hiring trends
    and
        AnalyticsPage->>API: GET /api/analytics/top-companies
        API->>Backend: Request company data
        Backend->>Aggregation: Aggregate by company
        Aggregation->>MongoDB: Pipeline:<br/>$group by company<br/>$count jobs<br/>$sort by count<br/>$limit 10
        MongoDB-->>Aggregation: Top companies
        Aggregation-->>Backend: Company rankings
        Backend-->>API: 200 OK + companies
        API-->>AnalyticsPage: Top companies
    and
        AnalyticsPage->>API: GET /api/analytics/salary-ranges
        API->>Backend: Request salary data
        Backend->>Aggregation: Aggregate salaries
        Aggregation->>MongoDB: Pipeline:<br/>$match salary exists<br/>$group by range<br/>$count
        MongoDB-->>Aggregation: Salary distribution
        Aggregation-->>Backend: Range data
        Backend-->>API: 200 OK + salaries
        API-->>AnalyticsPage: Salary ranges
    end
    
    AnalyticsPage->>AnalyticsPage: Render all charts
    AnalyticsPage->>User: Display dashboard
    
    %% Filter Analytics
    Note over User,Aggregation: Apply Time Filter
    User->>AnalyticsPage: Select "Last 30 days"
    AnalyticsPage->>API: GET /api/analytics/applications-stats?range=30d
    API->>Backend: Request with date filter
    Backend->>Aggregation: Add date filter to pipeline
    Aggregation->>MongoDB: $match createdAt >= 30 days ago
    MongoDB-->>Aggregation: Filtered results
    Aggregation-->>Backend: Filtered stats
    Backend-->>API: 200 OK + filtered data
    API-->>AnalyticsPage: Update data
    AnalyticsPage->>AnalyticsPage: Re-render charts
    AnalyticsPage->>User: Display updated analytics
    
    %% Drill Down
    Note over User,Aggregation: Drill Down on Company
    User->>AnalyticsPage: Click company in chart
    AnalyticsPage->>API: GET /api/analytics/company-details/:name
    API->>Backend: Request company breakdown
    Backend->>MongoDB: Find all jobs by company<br/>Find applications by company
    MongoDB-->>Backend: Jobs + applications
    Backend->>Backend: Calculate:<br/>- Total openings<br/>- Application rate<br/>- Response rate<br/>- Average time to interview
    Backend-->>API: 200 OK + company metrics
    API-->>AnalyticsPage: Company details
    AnalyticsPage->>User: Show detailed modal
    
    %% Compare Periods
    Note over User,Aggregation: Compare Time Periods
    User->>AnalyticsPage: Select "Compare to previous period"
    AnalyticsPage->>API: GET /api/analytics/compare?current=30d&previous=30d
    API->>Backend: Request comparison
    Backend->>Aggregation: Run two pipelines
    
    par Aggregate both periods
        Aggregation->>MongoDB: Current period pipeline
        MongoDB-->>Aggregation: Current stats
    and
        Aggregation->>MongoDB: Previous period pipeline
        MongoDB-->>Aggregation: Previous stats
    end
    
    Aggregation-->>Backend: Both datasets
    Backend->>Backend: Calculate deltas:<br/>% change for each metric
    Backend-->>API: 200 OK + comparison data
    API-->>AnalyticsPage: Comparison results
    AnalyticsPage->>User: Show trends with arrows
    
    %% Export Analytics
    Note over User,Aggregation: Export Analytics Report
    User->>AnalyticsPage: Click "Export Report"
    AnalyticsPage->>API: GET /api/analytics/export?format=pdf
    API->>Backend: Generate report
    Backend->>Aggregation: Fetch all metrics
    Aggregation->>MongoDB: Run all pipelines
    MongoDB-->>Aggregation: Complete dataset
    Aggregation-->>Backend: All analytics
    Backend->>Backend: Generate PDF report
    Backend-->>API: 200 OK + PDF blob
    API-->>AnalyticsPage: PDF file
    AnalyticsPage->>User: Download analytics.pdf
